   "he": "אָכְלָה כְּסוּת וְכוּ׳.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: If the animal «ate garments» or vessels, the owner must pay for half the cost of the damage. In what case is this statement said? It is said when the animal ate them while located on the property of the injured party, but if he ate them in the public domain the owner of the animal is exempt from liability."
